    "description": "Question-first tour of **Xray**, the re-frame2 devtools panel: how to *launch* it (inline in-app panel; the `open-overlay!` fallback for hosts with no `[data-rf-xray-host]` layout column; pop-out window; programmatic mount; the wired hotkeys), which of its two modes (Dynamic event-spine / Static registry browse) applies, and what each tab is for. **Do not use** when the user asks the AGENT to inspect or change their running app, read-only included (read a sub, snapshot state, walk traces, dispatch) — that is `re-frame2-pair`, the agent-facing runtime companion. Nor for authoring the host app (`re-frame2`), bootstrapping a project (`re-frame2-setup`), or implementing Xray itself (no implementor skill exists — the spec is the answer). Trigger phrases: \"open Xray\", \"which Xray panel shows…\", \"Xray Static mode\", \"browse registered machines/routes/schemas\", \"Xray overlay\", \"Xray machine inspector\", \"Xray Graph / Resources / Frames / Fresco tab\", \"why did this boundary re-render\".\n",
